   "evidence": "`ShortComplex` is a plain structure (`Mathlib/Algebra/Homology/ShortComplex/Basic.lean:34`), so projections of `ShortComplex.mk` reduce under simp; Mathlib's own `cokernelSequence`/`kernelSequence` are `@[simps]` (`Exact.lean:865-871`), but those field lemmas do not fire through the unexposed `upSES`/`downSES`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Induction/DimensionShift.lean",
   "fix": "Tag `upSES_def` and `downSES_def` `@[simp]`; simp then reduces the projections of the resulting `ShortComplex.mk`, giving `.f`, `.g` *and* `.X\u2081`/`.X\u2082`/`.X\u2083`. Drop the now-redundant `@[simp]` `upSES_X\u2081`/`_X\u2082`/`_X\u2083` and `downSES_X\u2081`/`_X\u2082`/`_X\u2083` (lines 90, 94, 98, 147, 151, 155), which is also what removes the simpNF duplication the PR description cites as the reason for not tagging `_def`.",
   "issue": "`upSES_def` (and `downSES_def`, line 141) is the only lemma that can reach `(upSES A).f`/`.g`, since `upSES_f`/`upSES_g` are unstateable with the body unexposed, but it carries no `@[simp]`. Downstream a goal mentioning `(upSES A).f` cannot be normalized by `simp`/`dsimp` at all (the body is not exposed, so simp cannot unfold `upSES`); it needs an explicit `rw [upSES_def]`.",
   "line": 84
  }
 ],
