 "summary": "Surface is minimal, bodies unexposed, and the universal properties (`up\u03c0IsCokernel`/`down\u03b9IsKernel`) plus zero-composite lemmas make the definitions usable without unfolding. The one gap is automation: with the bodies hidden, `(upSES A).f`/`.g` and `(downSES A).f`/`.g` have no simp route at all, because the only lemma that reaches them (`upSES_def`/`downSES_def`) is not `@[simp]`.",
